// === NAME - DESCRIPTION: Build the PDF from a Sum Table - Count the equally likely pairs from two spins or rolls, then use the table of sums to find P(X = k) and P(X >= m) ===
// === SET QUESTION TYPE TO: multipart ===

// === COMMON CONTROL ===

// Six scenarios (4-section spinner, 5-section spinner, six-sided die; X is the sum of the two numbers; two targets each).
// Parts: (a) numfunc - number of equally likely pairs; (b) numfunc - P(X = k); (c) numfunc - P(X >= m).
// Figure: a sum table, first number down the side, second number across the top, every cell the sum.
// Invariant: a sum s has n - |s - (n + 1)| pairs out of n x n; counts come from the generator, not hand work.

$anstypes = array("numfunc", "numfunc", "numfunc")

$ctxs = array("A spinner has 4 equal sections numbered 1 to 4. You spin it twice. `X` is the sum of the two numbers.", "A spinner has 4 equal sections numbered 1 to 4. You spin it twice. `X` is the sum of the two numbers.", "A spinner has 5 equal sections numbered 1 to 5. You spin it twice. `X` is the sum of the two numbers.", "A spinner has 5 equal sections numbered 1 to 5. You spin it twice. `X` is the sum of the two numbers.", "A fair six-sided die is rolled twice. `X` is the sum of the two numbers.", "A fair six-sided die is rolled twice. `X` is the sum of the two numbers.")
